    "recreation_brief": "1. Set the canvas to 960x540 px with background #FFFFFF; treat all boxes as normalized [x_min,y_min,x_max,y_max] coordinates and multiply x by 960 and y by 540 for pixels. 2. Draw the outer frame as a rectangle at [0.063,0.078,0.932,0.939] with fill #FFFFFF and border #C00000. 3. Draw the badge as a rounded box at [0.893,0.089,0.925,0.149] with fill #FFFF00 and outline #000000/#333333 (use #000000 if a single hex is required); center the bold dark numeral '4' inside it. 4. Place the title 'Quadratic Coefficients' centered in [0.358,0.111,0.657,0.169], bold, #C00000, about 22 pt, sans-serif. 5. Place the subtitle 'Two Variables Example' left-aligned in [0.083,0.185,0.286,0.224], italic, underlined, #C00000, smaller than the title, sans-serif. 6. Draw the top equation panel as a rectangle at [0.076,0.248,0.869,0.520] with fill #FFFFFF and border #C00000; left-align these 3 lines exactly: '(x_1  x_2) [[a_11  a_12],[a_21  a_22]] (x_1;x_2) = (a_11 x_1 + a_21 x_2   a_12 x_1 + a_22 x_2) (x_1;x_2)', '= (a_11 x_1 + a_21 x_2)x_1 + (a_12 x_1 + a_22 x_2)x_2 = a_11 x_1^2 + a_21 x_1 x_2 + a_12 x_1 x_2 + a_22 x_2^2', '= a_11 x_1^2 + (a_21 + a_12)x_1 x_2 + a_22 x_2^2 \\Rightarrow Quadratic form'; color x variables #FF0000, a coefficients #0000FF, other math ink #000000, and 'Quadratic form' #008000. 7. Draw the middle coefficient-mapping panel as a rectangle at [0.076,0.544,0.869,0.713] with fill #FFFFFF and border #C00000; left-align these 3 lines exactly: 'a_11 \\Rightarrow Coefficient of x_1^2', 'a_21 + a_12 \\Rightarrow Coefficient of x_1 x_2 \\Rightarrow a_12 = a_21 = 1/2 Coefficient of x_1 x_2', 'a_22 \\Rightarrow Coefficient of x_2^2'; color the \\Rightarrow arrows and 'a_12 = a_21 = 1/2' #0000FF and the 'Coefficient of ...' text #000000. 8. Draw the bottom matrix-to-coefficient panel as a rectangle at [0.076,0.731,0.869,0.917] with fill #FFFFFF and border #C00000. 9. Inside the bottom panel, place the column labels 'x_1' and 'x_2' above the two columns and the row labels 'x_1' and 'x_2' to the left of the two rows in #FF0000. 10. Inside the bottom panel, draw the left 2x2 matrix with black bracket cells containing row 1 'a_11', 'a_12' and row 2 'a_21', 'a_22'; color the a coefficients #0000FF. 11. Place a rightward '\\Rightarrow' in #0000FF between the left and right matrices. 12. Draw the right 2x2 coefficient matrix with black boxed cells containing row 1 'coef of x_1^2', '0.5 coef of x_1 x_2' and row 2 '0.5 coef of x_1 x_2', 'coef of x_2^2'; color the diagonal text #000000 and the off-diagonal '0.5 coef of x_1 x_2' text #0000FF. 13. Use sans-serif for the title, subtitle, badge, and labels; use serif-italic for math; keep panel text left-aligned except the centered title and badge. 14. Do not add animations; render the slide as static.",
