r a tight cluster of 2-3 to reflect the plural 'red dots').\n12. LEFT CALLOUT: Create 1 white box with red #E74C3C border (~1.5 pt) and red #E74C3C text 'Non-Linear Decision Boundary' at the left side of the chart band, vertically near the blue line; draw 1 straight red #E74C3C arrow from the box's right edge to the BLUE horizontal line (mapping exactly as extracted from source).\n13. RIGHT CALLOUT: Create 1 identical-style box with text 'Linear Decision Boundary' at the right side of the chart band; draw 1 straight red #E74C3C arrow from the box's left edge to the ORANGE parabola (mapping exactly as extracted from source).\n14. FINAL CHECK: The slide contains no other text, no equations, and no photos; everything is static (no animations). Verify all verbatim texts are present exactly: 'Non-Linearly Separable Data', 'Each Sample is represented by one features \"x\"', 'Non-Linear Decision Boundary', 'Linear Decision Boundary', 'x', '15'.",
