    "recreation_brief": "1. Set the slide background fill to white (#FFFFFF).\n2. Draw a rectangle for the outer frame with stroke #C00000 and no fill at [0.047, 0.061, 0.953, 0.941].\n3. Add a centered text box at [0.205, 0.08, 0.795, 0.14] with bold black (#000000) text \"Quadratic Kernel Mapping and Kernel Trick\" at approximately 22 pt.\n4. Draw a yellow (#FFFF00) filled circle at [0.878, 0.06, 0.935, 0.13] and place black text \"26\" centered inside it.\n5. Draw a rectangle with stroke #2E5AAC and no fill for the upper math box at [0.048, 0.15, 0.952, 0.507].\n6. Inside the upper math box, draw a salmon (#FCE4D6) filled rectangle at [0.063, 0.212, 0.398, 0.328] to highlight the leading identity term.\n7. Inside the upper math box, add the following four equation lines in serif italic math font (~12 pt), coloring a-terms red (#C00000), b-terms blue (#0000C0), and \u03c6 black (#000000): \"a = (a1; a2)   b = (b1; b2)\"; \"[a^T b]^2 = (a1 a2; b1 b2) = (a1 b1 + a2 b2)^2 = a1^2 b1^2 + a2^2 b2^2 + 2 a1 b1 a2 b2\"; \"[a^T b]^2 = (a1^2 a2^2 \u221a2 a1 a2 ; b1^2 b2^2 \u221a2 b1 b2) = \u03c6(a)^T \u03c6(b)\"; \"\u03c6(x) \u2261 (x1; x2) \u21d2 (x1^2; x2^2; \u221a2 x1 x2)\".\n8. Draw a vertical line with color #BFBFBF at x=0.615 from y=0.15 to y=0.505 inside the upper math box.\n9. Add black text \"Where:\" at [0.625, 0.26, 0.905, 0.48] in the right column of the upper math box.\n10. Add bold red (#C00000) text \"2D \u21d2 3D\" at [0.795, 0.462, 0.905, 0.5].\n11. Draw a rectangle with stroke #C00000 and no fill for the lower exercise box at [0.048, 0.515, 0.952, 0.905].\n12. Inside the lower exercise box, draw a rectangle with stroke #2E5AAC and no fill for the inner computation box at [0.062, 0.54, 0.902, 0.762].\n13. Inside the inner computation box at [0.052, 0.55, 0.2, 0.675], add the text \"a = (1; 2)   b = (3; 4)\" in serif italic math font (~12 pt) with a-terms red (#C00000) and b-terms blue (#0000C0).\n14. Inside the inner computation box at [0.205, 0.545, 0.905, 0.76], add the text \"\u03c6(a)^T \u03c6(b) = (1^2 2^2 \u221a2 1*2)(3^2; 4^2; \u221a2 3*4) = (1 4 \u221a2 2)(9; 16; \u221a2 12) = 9+64+48 = 121\" in serif italic math font (~12 pt) with \u03c6 in black (#000000).\n15. Draw a red (#C00000) left-pointing arrow glyph at [0.9, 0.555, 0.945, 0.615] aligned with the first \"121\" result.\n16. Inside the lower exercise box at [0.56, 0.795, 0.905, 0.875], add the text \"[a^T b]^2 = (1*3 + 2*4)^2 = 11^2 = 121\" in serif italic math font (~12 pt).\n17. Draw a red (#C00000) left-pointing arrow glyph at [0.898, 0.815, 0.945, 0.875] aligned with the second \"121\" result.",
