rox. x 13%-51%, y 38%-45%), place a peach (#FDEADA) filled rectangle with a thin orange (#FF9900) border containing 'Class of vector Z \u21d2 sign(W^T Z + b)': 'Class of vector', 'sign(', and '+ b)' in black, 'Z' in bold green, '\u21d2' in red.\n12. Behind 'W^T Z' inside the upper class strip, place a light-green (#CCFFCC) rounded rectangle with a green (#00CC00) outline (approx. x 40%-48%, y 39%-44%).\n13. Draw the kernelization connector strip at middle (approx. x 30%-62%, y 49%-56%): a thin red (#E00000) outlined rounded rectangle with white fill.\n14. Inside the left half of the connector strip, place italic black sans-serif text 'Kernelize using' (~13 pt).\n15. Inside the right half of the connector strip, place a separate red (#E00000) outlined rectangle containing bold red serif math text 'K(\u03b1,b) = \u03b1^T b^2'.\n16. Place a vertical downward-pointing arrow centered at approx. x 43%-45%, extending from y 47% to y 59%, with white fill and red (#E00000) outline, slim shaft with triangular head, connecting the connector strip to the lower panel.\n17. Draw the lower panel: a white rectangle with a thin blue (#0000CC) border spanning approx. x 7%-92%, y 61%-91%.\n18. Inside the lower panel on line 1, typeset the serif math equation '\u2112_D(\u03b1) = \u03a3_{i=1}^{N} \u03b1_i \u2212 1/2 \u03a3_{j=1}^{N} \u03a3_{i=1}^{N} \u03b1_i \u03b1_j y_i y_j (X_i^T X_j)^2' with the same color coding as step 6.\n19. Behind the final term '(X_i^T X_j)^2' in the lower dual objective, place a light-green (#CCFFCC) rounded rectangle with a green (#00CC00) outline (approx. x 43%-52%, y 64%-70%).\n20. Inside the lower panel on line 2 left (approx. x 9%-25%), place a white rectangle with a thin blue (#0000CC) border containing 'W = \u03a3_{i=1}^{N} \u03b1_i y_i X_i': W in bold blue, \u03b1_i y_i X_i in bold red.\n21. Inside the lower panel on line 2 right (approx. x 34%-90%), place a white rectangle with a thin blue (#0000CC) border containing 'b = \u2212 1/2 { max_{i,y=\u22121} [W^T X_i]^2 + min_{i,y=+1} [W^T X_i]^2 }': b in bold blue, max/min in red italic.\n22. Behind each '[W^T X_i]^2' term inside the lower b equation, place a light-green (#CCFFCC) rounded rectangle with a green (#00CC00) outline (approx. x 53%-82%, y 73%-79%).\n23. Inside the lower panel on line 3 (approx. x 13%-57%, y 83%-90%), place a peach (#FDEADA) filled rectangle with a thin orange (#FF9900) border containing 'Class of vector Z is sign([W^T Z]^2 + b)': 'Class of vector', 'is', 'sign(', and '+ b)' in black, 'Z' in bold green.\n24. Behind '[W^T Z]^2' inside the lower class strip, place a light-green (#CCFFCC) rounded rectangle with a green (#00CC00) outline (approx. x 43%-52%, y 84%-89%).\n25. Optionally overlay a small white mouse-pointer cursor with gray (#808080) outline, angled up-left, at approx. x 63%, y 78%, just left of the min_{i,y=+1} term in the lower b equation, to reproduce the video-capture artifact.\n26. Optionally add a solid black (#000000) horizontal bar across the very bottom edge (approx. x 4%-100%, y 96%-100%) only if reproducing the video screenshot rather than the clean slide.",
